{
  "esm": "2.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "transport_flux_divergence",
    "description": "B-grid lowering rule of the conservative flux-form tracer divergence rewrite target D(c*u, x) + D(c*v, y) for a per-category tracer c on the T cells advected by the B-grid corner velocities uvel/vvel on the U points: the rule matches the compound two-term sum with params c/u/v as wildcards and where-shape constraints (c: [i,j,ncat], u: [i,j], v: [i,j], esm-spec 9.6.1) and emits the [i,j,ncat] makearray of the conservative cell divergence div = (F_e(i,j,k) - F_e(i-1,j,k) + F_n(i,j,k) - F_n(i,j-1,k)) / tarea(i,j) (the Fortran mass update mm = mm - (mflxe(i,j) - mflxe(i-1,j) + mflxn(i,j) - mflxn(i,j-1))*tarear, ice_transport_remap.F90:3586-3590), where the east/north edge fluxes are the centered corner-average reconstructions F_e = HTE*((uS + uN)/2)*((cL + cR)/2) and F_n = HTN*((vW + vE)/2)*((cS + cN)/2) of the scalar atoms transport_flux_e/n: the edge runs between the two corner U points and its velocity is the average of the two corner velocities times the edge length, exactly the Fortran's edge-area reconstruction (edgearea_e/edgearea_n, ice_transport_remap.F90:658-666, the linear branch), and cL/cR (cS/cN) are the tracer values in the two cells sharing the edge, averaged to the face. The makearray tiles nine i/j position classes (interior [2..N_I-1]x[2..N_J-1], the four strips i = 1, i = N_I, j = 1, j = N_J, and the four corners) with halo-copy closures: every neighbor index that leaves the domain (c, u/v, HTE/HTN at i-1, i+1, j-1, j+1) is bound to the nearest interior value, reproducing the Fortran's ice_HaloUpdate of the transported fields and edge lengths. NOTE: the traced Fortran run integrates the incremental-remap transport (departure-region integrals over the limited linear reconstruction, transport_integrals, ice_transport_remap.F90:3188-3472), whose per-cell flux differs from this centered face average by O(C) slope corrections; the scheme difference is documented with the stage-2 transport pins.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:cice_bgrid",
      "grid:cice_bgrid",
      "op:D",
      "axes:i,j,ncat",
      "order:1",
      "form:flux",
      "bc:halo-copy",
      "stagger:b",
      "spec:9.6.8"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Hunke, E. C., et al. (2023). CICE v6.3.22 documentation and user's guide (LA-UR-23-31851), the horizontal transport edge reconstruction."
      }
    ]
  },
